    {
      "body": "> @janbernloehr which container did you use to validate this? I think this OOM was resolved with a TE upgrade to TE 2.20.\r\n\r\nThe validation used TE `2.20.2+6ea2a74a`, PyTorch `2.15.0a0+875d815502`, CUDA 13.5, Megatron-Bridge c0e164e, and MCore a0f793d.\r\n\r\nI also checked the latest runs from October 7–9. All three already use TE 2.20.2 and still OOM with cuda_graph_impl=full_iteration in DistributedOptimizer.copy_group_grads after two completed iterations. The failing runs hold 101.02 GiB in CUDA-graph private pools, so the TE upgrade has not resolved this particular workload’s OOM.\r\n\r\nWith TE-scoped graphs on attn, moe_router, and moe_preprocess, all eight ranks completed 30 iterations with finite losses and no skipped/NaN steps; the graph pool dropped to 33.684 GiB. That validation used CLI overrides on the earlier Bridge revision above. The exact PR commit still needs GPU validation.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T15:26:29Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/pull/6364#issuecomment-6083940522",
      "id": 6083940522,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T15:26:29Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "janbernloehr"
      }
    },
